# Normalise line endings so byte-for-byte comparisons do not depend on platform.
#
# The Move fixtures under src/__fixtures__/move are imported with `?raw` and
# compared against emitter output, which is always LF. Without an attribute, a
# Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true receives them as CRLF and
# src/__tests__/compiler/emitter.test.ts and pipeline.test.ts fail locally while
# passing in CI. The vendored sources under public/upstream-sources are already
# LF in the index and are covered by the same rule.
*.move text eol=lf

# Graph fixtures and the deploy-grade resolution snapshots are regenerated by
# scripts and reviewed as diffs. Pinning them to LF keeps a regeneration on
# Windows from rewriting every line.
*.json text eol=lf

# bun.lock is parsed line-by-line by the scripts/security/*.mjs regression
# suites with $-anchored regexes. A CRLF checkout leaves a trailing carriage
# return on every line, so no package row parses at all and `bun run
# test:security` fails on Windows with four assertion errors that look like
# missing lockfile entries.
bun.lock text eol=lf
